<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>T243 comparison — calendar-of-days panel</title>
<style>
  html,body{margin:0;padding:0;background:#181818;font-family:Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;color:#fff}
  #wrap{display:flex;gap:10px;width:min(98vw,1100px);margin:10px auto;align-items:flex-start}
  .side{flex:1;min-width:0}
  .side h2{font-size:15px;margin:4px 0 8px;text-align:center}
  video{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;background:#000}
  #rec{width:100%}
  #rec svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}
  #ctl{width:min(96vw,640px);margin:8px auto 16px;display:flex;gap:8px;justify-content:center}
  button{font-size:16px;padding:10px 18px;border-radius:8px;border:2px solid #888;background:#2a2a2a;color:#fff;cursor:pointer;min-height:44px}
  @media (max-width:560px){ #wrap{flex-direction:column} .side{width:100%} }
</style></head><body>
<div id="wrap">
  <div class="side"><h2>ORIGINAL — ensan.besham Hope = Failure (?) @ 13–27 s</h2><video id="vid" src="segment.mp4" playsinline preload="auto"></video></div>
  <div class="side"><h2>RECREATION — T243 Calendar-of-days panel, parameterized</h2><div id="rec"></div></div>
</div>
<div id="ctl"><button id="playBtn" type="button">Play</button><button id="restartBtn" type="button">Restart</button></div>
<script>
"use strict";
// Anchor map: cut-relative video seconds -> build ms. Build knots are DERIVED from recreation.html's CONFIG at runtime.
let T243 = null, KNOTS = [[0,0],[15,12400]];
fetch("recreation.html").then(r => r.text()).then(txt => {
  const m = txt.match(/<script>([\s\S]*?)<\/script>/);
  const cut = m[1].split("if (typeof document")[0];
  const f2 = new Function(cut.replace("window.__T243", "window.__T243CMP") + "; return window.__T243CMP;");
  T243 = f2();
  const S = T243.schedule(T243.CONFIG);
  KNOTS = [[0,0],[4.5,S.gridStart + T243.CONFIG.gridDurMs],[6.5,S.labelsStart + T243.CONFIG.labelsDurMs],[8.5,S.tasksStart + T243.CONFIG.tasksDurMs],[10.5,S.sweep3Start + T243.CONFIG.sweep3DurMs],[12.5,S.finalStart + T243.CONFIG.finalDurMs],[15,S.durationMs]];
  document.getElementById("rec").innerHTML = T243.renderSVG(T243.CONFIG, 0);
});
function buildMsAt(videoSec){
  for (let k = 0; k < KNOTS.length - 1; k++){
    const a = KNOTS[k], b = KNOTS[k+1];
    if (videoSec <= b[0]){ return a[1] + (b[1]-a[1]) * ((videoSec - a[0]) / (b[0] - a[0])); }
  }
  return KNOTS[KNOTS.length-1][1];
}
const vid = document.getElementById("vid");
const recEl = document.getElementById("rec");
let playing = false, frozenSec = 0;
function frame(){
  if (!playing) return;
  const sec = vid.ended ? 15 : vid.currentTime;
  if (T243) recEl.innerHTML = T243.renderSVG(T243.CONFIG, buildMsAt(sec));
  if (vid.ended){ playing = false; document.getElementById("playBtn").textContent = "Play"; return; }
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
}
document.getElementById("playBtn").addEventListener("click", function(){
  if (playing){ playing = false; frozenSec = vid.currentTime; vid.pause(); this.textContent = "Play"; return; }
  playing = true; this.textContent = "Pause";
  if (vid.ended){ vid.currentTime = 0; }
  vid.play(); requestAnimationFrame(frame);
});
document.getElementById("restartBtn").addEventListener("click", function(){
  playing = true; vid.currentTime = 0; vid.play();
  document.getElementById("playBtn").textContent = "Pause"; requestAnimationFrame(frame);
});
</script></body></html>
### T243 — Calendar-of-days panel with crossed-out dates (P14 T04) ◆ — OWED #108
- Tier: **DESCRIBED — OWED #108**
- Mechanics: a rounded panel holds a grid of day numerals; most are struck through with diagonal slashes, two are ringed, and dashed drop-lines connect two crossed dates to a timeline below whose labels are also struck out; a second panel with empty checkboxes joins it. Draw-on order: grid → strikes → drop-lines → timeline labels — "after such-and-such a date it will work out" is refuted by the calendar itself. (Named draw-on order — OWED.)
- Feeds: diagram · transition — P14 @ ≈13–27 s — ev/020-calendar-days.jpg, ev/026-calendar-tasks-crossout.jpg

### T246 — Resource bars over standing figures (day-2 depletion scene) (P14 T07)
- Tier: **DESCRIBED — not owed**
- Mechanics: three figures stand in a row; above each, a tall thin bar outline stands nearly empty, with a small filled segment at the base of the middle bar; below, an empty rounded report panel waits. The bars do not animate down on screen — depletion is shown as an already-low state, held: day 2's losses are inventory, not events. (Held state, no motion — not owed, priced from the packet's own mechanics.)
- Feeds: diagram — P14 @ ≈49–58 s — ev/050-day2-resource-bars.jpg


